    <GaugingStation location="Fosseway" name="Sherston Avon" number="53023">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V Crump profile weir installed in 1976. Artificial influences produced lowest flows on record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Full range station. Fossebridge upstream used for gauging flows. Theoretical rating applied across period of record. Bypassing found at high flows, and will be modelled.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Station is located 3km upstream of Malmsbury and was opened in 1976. Flat V Crump profile weir, crest 7m broad.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff heavily influenced by groundwater abstraction/recharge. Artificial influences produced lowest flows on record in 11/1978. Flows augmented by ground water scheme with minor augmentation from effluent returns. Stream support upstream. Gate activity upstream may affect flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Geology: The catchment upstream is predominantly Oolitic limestone with Coal Measures. Land use is rural.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">G</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Reasonable fit to gauging." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 14% of AMAX3. Rating is thought to perform reasonably beyond QMED." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
